1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,000
WuWa VR: an unofficial, free fan mod that plays Wuthering Waves on a PC VR headset.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
It turns the game's single flat camera into two eye views with head tracking.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
The game renders a normal Unreal Engine camera, world and UI.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
UEVR plus our native hooks redirect the scene and the real game UI. Lua scripts handle camera, body and controls.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
A VR runtime (OpenXR) receives two eyes: the same moment, from slightly different viewpoints.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
19–26 Sep: real game UI in VR, first person, head, body and shadow improvements.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
27 Sep: turning Native Stereo Fix on repaired character materials (owner-reported).

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Real progress on specific screens and cases, not a finished stereo renderer.

9
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Still open: one tree animates in both eyes up close…

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
…but freezes in the left eye far away, even with zero eye separation and equal projection scale.

11
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Also open: ultimate transitions (candidate not yet accepted), reflection submenus, some shadows.

12
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Next: name the actual failing asset, then compare what each eye's draw really receives.

13
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Then make the smallest proven fix, and test everything together in one grouped pass.

14
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Free and experimental. Source and beginner guide: github.com/ChronoHaxx/wuwa-vr

